# What stays out of a vault's Git history.
#
# Rule of thumb: if a file is written by Obsidian or a plugin as you use it,
# it is local state and does not belong here. It differs per machine, changes
# constantly, and causes merge conflicts that stall the Git plugin's sync.

# ---- Obsidian UI state ----
# These record which panes you have open, so they change every time you
# click around. Sharing them causes pointless merge conflicts.
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json

# ---- Per-device preferences ----
.obsidian/appearance.json
.obsidian/graph.json
.obsidian/hotkeys.json

# ---- Plugin settings: deny by default ----
# Plugins fill these in as you use them, and they may hold API keys (Excalidraw
# has slots for OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini and xAI) or absolute local paths
# (Pandoc's binary, Zotero's database). List an exception only for settings the
# team genuinely shares.
.obsidian/plugins/*/data.json
.obsidian/plugins/*/data.json.bak
.obsidian/plugins/obsidian-git/obsidian_askpass.sh

# The Git plugin's own settings ARE shared: this is how the sync configuration
# (pull on boot, pull before push, commit interval) reaches every machine.
!.obsidian/plugins/obsidian-git/data.json
#
# IMPORTANT - MOBILE USERS ONLY
# On phones and tablets the Git plugin cannot use SSH, so it stores your
# GitHub access token in that same file. If anyone sets that up, DELETE the
# exception line directly above immediately, so the token is never committed.
# You lose shared sync settings; that is the correct trade.

# ---- Local caches and generated artifacts ----
.smart-env/
.trash/
conflict-files-obsidian-git.md

# ---- AI assistant local state ----
# Session history may contain sensitive prompts; settings are personal
# (model, effort level, permission mode) and must not be pushed onto teammates.
.claudian/sessions/
.claudian/claudian-settings.json

# ---- Local credentials and key material ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ---- Operating system junk ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*~

# NOTE: we deliberately do NOT block large files here.
# If git silently ignored your spreadsheet you would never know why it
# failed to sync. Keeping big files out of this repo is a rule people
# follow, not a filter - see "Where things belong" in README.md.
